    "created_at": "2025-04-25T02:11:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-25T02:11:13Z",
    "body": "I think the current spec is probably good as-is.\n\nThe status quo is that we do fully-active checks on the promise handler's realm, in [check if we can run script](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#check-if-we-can-run-script) step 1 via [HostEnqueuePromiseJob](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hostenqueuepromisejob) step 2.1.\n\nWe do not check the promise's realm (partially since ECMAScript doesn't define a realm for generic objects). This can lead to some confusion like in #11252. But, the handler-realm-check is enough to prevent the infinite loop of the sort Boris points out in the original post.\n\nTo get an infinite loop in a situation similar to the OP, you need the same-origin B to grab a function from its opener A and use that in its infinite loop. And it's already the case that a same-origin openee can cause its opener to run an infinite loop, even after B closes. So as long as we avoid the case where very innocent B-only code can cause an infinite loop after B closes, I think we've done our job.\n\nFurthermore, the current spec has the benefit of allowing clear failure signals for active documents that call APIs on inactive documents. E.g., as discussed upthread in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2621#issuecomment-598232593, or as shown in [this web platform test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/6b1b6210cc781a4c5a854ed0ed139f3690e13e4a/navigation-api/navigation-methods/return-value/reload-rejection-order-detached-unserializablestate.html) (the subject of #11252).\n\nSince we are testing this at least indirectly in some tests like the above, I don't think there's much left to track here, so let me close this.\n\nWe can leave #1989 open to track a more general investigation into inactive document scripting. For example I know there's some interop issues around event handlers in inactive documents: https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1084",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
